  "notes": "USAGE:\n{面会|めんかい} is most commonly used for visiting someone in an institutional setting such as a hospital or prison. It has a more formal and structured nuance than a casual visit.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {面会|めんかい}する (to visit, to meet)\n- {面会|めんかい}{時間|じかん} (visiting hours)\n- {面会|めんかい}{謝絶|しゃぜつ} (no visitors allowed)\n- {面会|めんかい}に{行|い}く (to go visit)\n- {面会|めんかい}を{断|ことわ}る (to refuse a visit)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n{見舞|みま}い focuses on visiting someone who is ill to wish them well, while {面会|めんかい} is the broader, more formal term for any institutional visit.",
